Z||000000||Ghia||10-16-2000||12:13 PM||||I have a 87GT and I'm going to put wider rims on the rear of the car.  Has anyone used the Carrera coil-over kit and how does it compare to the Ryane kit?<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||10
Z||000001||Wade87GT||10-16-2000||12:40 PM||||Hello Ghia,<P>Can't help you with a comparison but I'm in the middle of a complete suspension upgrade using tubular control arms and coil-overs that I bought from RCC. The fronts use Carrera shocks and the rears use Gabriel struts. HAL springs are all around. Every part I received from RCC is well made and almost too beautiful to hide behind wheels (I'm a tech guy). Also, the tech support from them has been 100%. I should be rolling by the end of the week. If you'd like an update after that, let me know.<P>Wade||||reg||1
Z||000002||1FST2M6||10-16-2000||02:21 PM||||i haven't used the Fiero specic kit but we have used Carrera kits in the race cars at the shop for MANY years! they have a great product and AWSOME service!   welcome to the forum!<P> <A HREF="http://www.engineered.net" TARGET=_blank>www.engineered.net</A> <P>------------------<BR>Shhh.. Top Secret! <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fstcheeto_2.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 10-16-2000).]||||reg||1
